[al:新概念英语第一册]
[ar:Louis G.Alexander]
[ti:143. A Walk Through the Woods]
[by:Generated by iChochy]

[00:00.000]Lesson 143 | 第143课
[00:05.350]I live in a very old town /taʊn/, which is surrounded /səˈraʊndɪd/ by beautiful woods /wʊdz/. | 我住在一个很古老的小镇上，那里四周环绕着美丽的树林。
[00:12.190]It is a famous beauty spot /ˈbjuːti spɒt/. | 它是一个著名的风景区。
[00:15.220]On Sundays, hundreds /ˈhʌndrədz/ of people come from the city to see our town /taʊn/ and to walk through /θruː/ the woods /wʊdz/. | 每逢星期天，数以百计的人从城里来到我们的小镇参观，并在树林中散步。
[00:24.490]Visitors /ˈvɪzɪtəz/ have been asked to keep the woods /wʊdz/ clean and tidy /ˈtaɪdi/. | 游客们被要求保持树林整洁。
[00:30.300]Litter /ˈlɪtə/ baskets /ˈbɑːskɪts/ have been placed /pleɪst/ under the trees. | 树下放了废纸篓。
[00:34.780]But people still throw /θrəʊ/ their rubbish /ˈrʌbɪʃ/ everywhere. | 但人们仍然随处乱扔垃圾。
[00:39.370]Last Wednesday, I went for a walk in the woods /wʊdz/. | 上星期三，我到树林里散步。
[00:45.180]What I saw made me very sad /sæd/. | 我所见到的一切让我非常难过。
[00:49.950]I counted /ˈkaʊntɪd/ seven old cars and three old refrigerators. | 我数了数，有7辆旧汽车和3台旧冰箱。
[00:56.240]The litter /ˈlɪtə/ baskets /ˈbɑːskɪts/ were empty. | 废纸篓是空的。
[00:59.580]And the ground /ɡraʊnd/ was covered /ˈkʌvəd/ with pieces of paper, cigarette ends /endz/, old tires /taɪəz/, empty bottles and rusty /ˈrʌsti/ tins. | 地上铺满了碎纸、烟头、旧轮胎、空瓶子和生锈的罐头盒。
[01:11.390]Among the rubbish /ˈrʌbɪʃ/, I found a sign which said, | 在这些垃圾中，我发现了一块牌子，上面写着：
[01:17.370]“Anyone who leaves litter /ˈlɪtə/ in these woods /wʊdz/ will be prosecuted /ˈprɒsɪkjuːtɪd/.” | “凡在此树林里乱扔垃圾者，将受到法律的制裁。”
